{
  "id": "Compound::DB00655 - Gene::1544",
  "verbalization": "Estrone is implicated in the regulation of Cyp1a2 through its interaction with Cyp2c9 and Cyp3a4, which both participate in oxidoreductive activities involving quinone or similar acceptors. These activities are central to the metabolic activation of xenobiotics, and Cyp1a2 is a key enzyme in this process. The evidence suggests that Estrone binds to Cyp2c9 and Cyp3a4, which in turn contribute to the enzymatic activity of Cyp1a2. This indicates a potential mechanism by which Estrone influences Cyp1a2 function, likely through modulating the activity of its substrates. The overlapping roles of Cyp2c9 and Cyp3a4 in the same metabolic pathway support the idea that Estrone may act as a modulator of Cyp1a2, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
